3D world of the NiFT web playground

world.glb, height.bin.gz and trees.json are derived from the digital twin published at https://github.com/mcity/mcity-digital-twin (tag 1.9.1, the USD copy in Omniverse/), which is MIT licensed. Its notice is reproduced below as that license requires. The files were made with nift_playground/tools/world3d/build_world.sh.

What was changed: the static world (ground, roads, curbs, markings, buildings, props, signs, poles, traffic and street lights) was converted to glTF, moved into the NiFT map frame, given one flat colour per surface and compressed. No textures are included. Left out on purpose: every surface that carries a logo or a brand (street light banners, the roundabout disc, wrapped electrical boxes, a mailbox, a painted rock, a shuttle stop sign, tunnel signage), the plant cards of the GPS blocker, and all foliage. The trees the page draws are our own simple shapes, placed at the positions and species of the twin's plants (trees.json). Brand names were removed from all names in the files.

